<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <div class="hero">
    <span class="chapter">Prepare Second Edition Level 3 &middot; Units 13 and 14</span>
    <h1 class="big">Present Perfect Quest</h1>
    <p>Four stops, one grammar: <b>have</b> or <b>has</b> plus the past participle. Start with the rules, cross the two Grammar: Plus worksheets, and train the irregular verbs in the vault until they are yours.</p>
    <div class="verbline">ever &middot; never &middot; just &middot; already &middot; yet</div>
  </div>

  <p class="maplead"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 7.5l4 3.2L12 4l5 6.7 4-3.2-1.9 11.3H4.9z"/></svg> The map of the quest</p>

  <div class="map">

    <section class="stop">
      <span class="num">Stop I</span>
      <h2>The Hall of Ever and Never</h2>
      <p>The grammar of Unit 13 first: the four forms of the present perfect, the seven rules of the book, and then three trials. Write the past participles, build statements with <b>never</b>, and ask questions with <b>ever</b>.</p>
      <div class="what"><span>Unit 13</span><span>Grammar reference</span><span>3 trials</span></div>
      <a class="enter" href="present-perfect-ever-never-unit13.html">Enter</a>
    </section>

    <section class="stop">
      <span class="num">Stop II</span>
      <h2>The Trials of Ever and Never</h2>
      <p>The Grammar: Plus worksheet of Unit 13, with all five written exercises. Choose between <b>ever</b> and <b>never</b>, turn loose words into sentences, use the verb box, hunt the mistakes, and finish the camping conversation.</p>
      <div class="what"><span>Unit 13</span><span>Grammar Plus</span><span>5 trials</span></div>
      <a class="enter" href="unit13-grammar-plus.html">Enter</a>
    </section>

    <section class="stop">
      <span class="num">Stop III</span>
      <h2>The Market of Just, Already and Yet</h2>
      <p>The Grammar: Plus worksheet of Unit 14. Three new words join the present perfect and each one has its own place in the sentence. Rewrite, build, match, correct and complete Henry's text.</p>
      <div class="what"><span>Unit 14</span><span>Grammar Plus</span><span>5 trials</span></div>
      <a class="enter" href="unit14-grammar-plus.html">Enter</a>
    </section>

    <section class="stop">
      <span class="num">Stop IV</span>
      <h2>The Vault of Irregular Verbs</h2>
      <p>A game, not a worksheet. Twenty-nine irregular verbs from these two units, one at a time and against the clock. Choose the past participle, keep your streak alive, and beat your own best run.</p>
      <div class="what"><span>Units 13 and 14</span><span>Speed run</span><span>29 verbs</span></div>
      <a class="enter" href="speed-run-irregular-participles.html">Enter</a>
    </section>

  </div>

  <section class="card codex">
    <span class="tag">The old shelf</span>
    <h2>Earlier material</h2>
    <p class="sub">The irregular past simple chapters and the reading trivia. They belong to another unit, but they live in the same folder, so here are their doors.</p>
    <div class="shelf">
      <a href="01-groups-1-2-3.html">Past simple &middot; Groups 1, 2 and 3</a>
